n><span><span><span>🐰 Hoppin and poppin<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Sierra Nevada Northern Hemisphere Harvest</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Wet Hopped IPA<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Hitachino Nest Daisy</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Pale Ale<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Maine Beer Little Whaleboat</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> IPA &amp; </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Peeper</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Pale Ale</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/2a22c5fd-5941-3685-9df3-70511a4a2a1f.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>👊 Goodies from </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Humble Forager</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Trail Buzz </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Brown Ale<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Driftless Drummer</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Wet Hop West Coast IPA with Krush &amp; Nelson Sauvin</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/1195d153-fe7b-6e4b-ac79-6b34a6a54986.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>⚡️Local energy<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Three Notch’d Blood Orange Gose</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Ardent Schwarzbier</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Fairwinds Texas Flood</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> West Coast IPA<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Right Proper Croquet Club</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> NZ IPA</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>Bear Chase Pumpkin Patches</p>\n<p>Black Hog Granola Brown</p>\n<p>Sojourn Ten Czech Pilsner</p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/4d6da500-27c5-cac6-5f60-6d16589262db.jpeg\" width=\"612\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><strong><span>Ultraviolet Blanc de Blancs Sparkling</span><span>: </span></strong><span><span><span><span>Another banger from Samantha Sheehan... and to think she was almost a tax attorney. Recognized as one of Food &amp; Wine Magazine's \"15 Women to Watch in Wine,\" Samantha uses only locally-grown, organically-farmed grapes while keeping production petite. Her new Blanc de Blancs sparkler is zesty and crisp with notes of citrus. The perfect aperitif! Organic.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Germans Balart Petitona Blanc</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span></span><span><span><span><span>Marc and Luís began their small family winery out of the basement of their grandparents' home in the historic center of Gandesa in the Terra Alta region — an up-and-coming appellation tucked in the hills of southern Catalonia. In 2020, they fled the nest to more modern facilities, but the wine is still hands-on and small production. Fermented in stainless steel, Petitona Blanc is a fresh and bright white blend with apple, pear, mango, and a touch of citrus that pairs with absolutely everything.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong>The Fableist Pinot Noir</strong>: <span><span><span><span>You may have noticed that we're big fans of Andrew Jones' The Fableist project. A California Pinot Noir that leans Burgundian in style with savory notes of thyme, cracked white pepper and forest mushrooms blends with pops of cranberry and strawberry. Native Yeast, Vegan &amp; Sustainable.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong>Mary Taylor Marine Descombe Morgon Beaujolais</strong>: <span><span><span><span>Our favorite importer Mary Taylor paired up with fellow wine trailblazer Marine Descombe for a Cru Beaujolais from Morgon. Marine took over her family winery — founded in 1905 by her grandfather, making her the fifth generation — before she was even 30 years old. Coming from the land of granitic schist soils, Morgon has plenty of old world charm with dark berries, violets and chewy tannins.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong>Germans Balart Petitona Red</strong>: <span><span><span><span>A bold and fun blend of 60% Garnatxa Negra and 40% Carinyena — two of Catalonia's most ancient and proudly indigenous red grapes. Aged only in stainless steel for a fruit-forward red that punches well above its weight with ripe dark berries, Mediterranean herbs, a touch of spice and soft rounded tannins.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/2fd7c676-a1f4-95b9-03b1-39b78a105359.jpeg\" width=\"612\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span><span><span>I have a real problem. I got off the library hold for four ebooks at one time. If you're familiar with the Libby system, you know that speed reading is in my weekend plans. And I suspect I'll read just a tad bit faster with a glass of fall-forward </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Macanita MAC Tinto</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> by my side.<br><br>Joana Maçanita is a bit of a mover-shaker in the Portuguese winemaking world, but before that she had a lengthy career as a gymnast on the Portuguese national team. You might say her talent is both flexible and unlimited. After her gymnastics career, Joana enrolled at the Instituto Superior de Agronomia for university, just like her brother and best friend, winemaker António. Working with her brother - hence the name MAC which is the nickname associated with their family name Maçanita - Joana sources grapes from high altitude vineyards throughout the Douro Valley.<br><br>Let me just say, MAC reminds me why I'm obsessed with reds from the Douro Valley. A blend of indigenous varieties Touriga Nacional, Sousão, and Tinta Rori, MAC is big on flavor, but not on weight. The wine finishes in both concrete and stainless steel rather than oak for a fresh, vibrant expression with ripe black fruit, dried herbs and a mineral finish. A fruit-forward, easy-drinking red ready to pair with hard cheese, grilled and smoked meat or a great book. And for those of you wondering, my TBR pile includes It Could Have Been Her, Demon Copperhead, Mad Mabel and First Time Caller.</span></span></span></p>\n<p><em><span><span><span><span>This week’s writeup is brought to you by Beth</span></span></span></span></em></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/44528625-75ce-77b6-246b-4628384a151b.jpeg\" width=\"612\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p>Thanks for your business! See you soon, Beth, Julie &amp; Aidan and the entire Brew Crew</p>",
